sections.text:
Every AI tool now wants the design system in its own format. The tools are cheap and change every month. What clients can't do alone:
- make a messy system readable to agents;
- keep all those formats in sync;
- prove the output stays on-system;
- govern what agents change.

That is the service.

Why they need us · Service line · Package · What exists today

A messy system isn't readable by agents · 1 · AI-readiness clean-up + score · 2-week AI audit → DS Accelerate · Partly: ASSA before/after, DSN index + absences, audits
8+ agent formats drift apart · 2 · One source, every agent channel · DS Accelerate · Partly: DSN MCP, 8 skills, llms.txt; generators per channel are new
Nobody can prove AI output is on-system · 3 · Evals + CI gates · Accelerate → Support · Partly: DSN audits, ASSA binding parity, Starter Pack a11y gate; eval harness is new
Agents now change the system · 4 · Agent governance · DS Scale / Support · Partly: Figma 3-way review, DSN PR flow, ASSA propose → confirm → apply
(foundation for everything) · 5 · DTCG token architecture · DS Build / Scale · Works: Starter Pack brands, ASSA Brand/Theme/Device
Their own AI features need a safe catalog · 6 · Generative UI catalog · Spike, outside MVP · Proposed
Unvetted CLIs and MCPs everywhere · 7 · Client toolchain + skills pack · Any package · Works: DSN CLI + skills, Starter Pack plugin
No people, no playbook, no ROI method · 8 · Enablement + ROI baseline · Support · Service: Handbook, decision map, ASSA metrics table

Commodity, don't sell alone:
- installing an MCP server;
- a theme configurator;
- a token export CLI;
- another docs site;
- chat over docs;
- one DESIGN.md file.
